### Define and Handle Firebase Functions Errors

Source: https://github.com/firebase/firebase-js-sdk/blob/main/common/api-review/functions.api.md

Defines custom error types for Firebase Functions, extending FirebaseError. Includes error codes and optional details.

```typescript
export class FunctionsError extends FirebaseError {
    constructor(
    code: FunctionsErrorCodeCore, message?: string,
    details?: unknown);
    readonly details?: unknown;
}

export type FunctionsErrorCode = `functions/${FunctionsErrorCodeCore}`;

export type FunctionsErrorCodeCore = 'ok' | 'cancelled' | 'unknown' | 'invalid-argument' | 'deadline-exceeded' | 'not-found' | 'already-exists' | 'permission-denied' | 'resource-exhausted' | 'failed-precondition' | 'aborted' | 'out-of-range' | 'unimplemented' | 'internal' | 'unavailable' | 'data-loss' | 'unauthenticated';
```

--------------------------------

### FunctionsError Constructor (TypeScript)

Source: https://github.com/firebase/firebase-js-sdk/blob/main/docs-devsite/functions.functionserror.md

Provides the constructor signature for the FunctionsError class. It accepts an error code, an optional message, and optional details for error reporting.

```typescript
constructor(
    code: FunctionsErrorCode,
    message?: string,
    details?: unknown
);
```

