### Firebase Functions Error Codes (TypeScript)

Source: https://github.com/firebase/firebase-js-sdk/blob/main/docs-devsite/functions.md

Defines the set of status codes for Firebase Functions, mirroring gRPC status codes. These codes indicate the outcome of function executions, from successful operations to various error conditions.

```typescript
export type FunctionsErrorCode = `functions/${FunctionsErrorCodeCore}`;
```

--------------------------------

### Firebase Functions Error Code Core Values (TypeScript)

Source: https://github.com/firebase/firebase-js-sdk/blob/main/docs-devsite/functions.md

Specifies the core string values for Firebase Functions error codes, which are appended after the 'functions/' prefix. This type lists all possible error states a function might return.

```typescript
export type FunctionsErrorCodeCore = 'ok' | 'cancelled' | 'unknown' | 'invalid-argument' | 'deadline-exceeded' | 'not-found' | 'already-exists' | 'permission-denied' | 'resource-exhausted' | 'failed-precondition' | 'aborted' | 'out-of-range' | 'unimplemented' | 'internal' | 'unavailable' | 'data-loss' | 'unauthenticated';
```

Source: https://github.com/firebase/firebase-js-sdk/blob/main/docs-devsite/functions.md

functions package > FunctionsErrorCodeCore: Functions error code string appended after "functions/" product prefix. See [FunctionsErrorCode](./functions.md#functionserrorcode) for full documentation of codes.
